From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: comctl32: list view groups and the tile view

Group view (LVM_ENABLEGROUPVIEW) and its groups -- LVM_INSERTGROUP,
LVM_INSERTGROUPSORTED, LVM_SETGROUPINFO/GETGROUPINFO/GETGROUPINFOBYINDEX,
LVM_REMOVEGROUP, LVM_REMOVEALLGROUPS, LVM_HASGROUP, LVM_GETGROUPCOUNT,
LVM_SORTGROUPS, LVM_GETGROUPRECT, LVM_GETGROUPSTATE, LVM_GETFOCUSEDGROUP,
LVM_SET/GETGROUPMETRICS, LVM_ISGROUPVIEWENABLED -- and an item's group
(LVIF_GROUPID, I_GROUPIDCALLBACK) in every view but List: the groups are laid
out top to bottom, each a header (the accent colour, a line to the edge, a
chevron when collapsible) and then its items as the view places them; an item
in no group is not shown, as on Windows. Clicking a header selects its items,
its chevron folds it. Arrow keys, Home/End and Page Up/Down move by where the
items are. The tile view (LV_VIEW_TILE, LVM_SET/GETTILEVIEWINFO,
LVM_SET/GETTILEINFO, LVIF_COLUMNS, LVM_SETTILEWIDTH): the large icon at the
left, the name and then a line per tile column in grey.

Gates: test/explorer2-gate.sh (grouped details view, tiles).
